1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,933
You log in.
Your password never reaches your agent.

2
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:06,933
You, to your agent: “The API on staging is down. Look at my terminal and get it running.”

3
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:08,534
It asks to join. Once.

4
00:00:08,534 --> 00:00:13,770
It picks up the shell you are already in.

5
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:23,431
On your server, every command waits for you.

6
00:00:23,431 --> 00:00:25,903
It wants to delete the whole cache.

7
00:00:25,903 --> 00:00:27,329
You say no.

8
00:00:27,329 --> 00:00:30,529
Then you just type.
Your keystroke takes the terminal back.

9
00:00:30,529 --> 00:00:34,029
You, to your agent: “I cleared the lock myself. Read the terminal and continue.”

10
00:00:34,029 --> 00:00:41,698
It reads what you did.

11
00:00:41,698 --> 00:00:46,650
And finishes the job.

12
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:52,050
Your agent works in your terminal. You keep the keyboard.
Real Conn, a real SSH login and a real Claude Code session in one continuous take. Prepared scenario; still moments shortened.
